    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance to help responders locate the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the single driveway entrance clearly so responders arriving under low-visibility conditions can identify it without delay.\n• Keep the access drive clear of parked vehicles so emergency apparatus can reach the property without obstruction.\n• Identify and communicate a secondary access point to the rear of the property, or arrange for a rear gate that can be opened quickly by responders if needed.\n• Trim vegetation along both sides of the access drive so it does not narrow the travel width or obstruct responder sightlines.\n• Cut back dense vegetation near the detached structures so responders can move around and between those buildings without obstruction.\n• Keep a clear path between the main structure and each detached structure so responders can move freely across the property.\n• Mark the water feature with a visible indicator so responders working in low-light or smoke conditions do not step into it.\n• Keep walkways clear of overgrown vegetation so responders can move quickly between areas of the property.\n• Thin dense plantings near the perimeter fencing so responders can identify fence openings and access points without searching through growth."
  },
