    "recommendations": "• Trim tree branches that hang over or touch any part of the structure.\n• Thin trees in the cluster nearest to the structure to create open space between individual trees.\n• Remove shrubs growing directly against or within a few feet of the structure's walls and foundation.\n• Clear brush from the area immediately surrounding the structure on all sides.\n• Cut grass near the structure short and keep it mowed regularly during dry periods.\n• Separate scattered shrubs from one another where they grow close together near the structure.\n• Remove dead plant material from within the mixed vegetation area closest to the structure.\n• Thin dense vegetation on the side of the property nearest the structure to open up space between plants.\n• Clear vegetation along the sides of the driveway so vehicles can pass through without obstruction.\n• Keep the driveway surface free of fallen branches and debris that could block emergency vehicle access.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so it is visible from the road for emergency responders.\n• Clear a path around the rear of the structure wide enough for a person to walk through safely.\n• Remove any piled or stacked flammable material stored near the structure such as wood, debris, or yard waste.\n• Keep the single access route clear of overhanging branches along its full length."
